    text: "First full coverage attempt after the operation-signal fix ran 9886 cases: 9882 passed, two Linux platform skips, and two failed. The packed continuation test lacked the test-process NODE_PATH required by this host; an unchanged repository-wide absence-gate test exceeded its 30s timeout. No coverage report was certified. Both affected suites then passed (20 cases) without source, timeout or threshold changes after exposing the verified global npm package through test-process NODE_PATH. Repeat the unchanged full canonical runner and strict gates before claiming final results; the timeout cause is unproven."
  - created_at: "2026-10-07T10:18:04.795Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final operation-identity verification: 9884 applicable tests pass, two Windows-only Linux skips, exact all-source 100/100/100/100 (67111 statements, 51380 branches, 13839 functions, 63953 lines). Full strict static gates and all four TypeScript projects pass; no denominator, exclusions, timeout or threshold changed. Latest pm-changelog remains 2026.10.5. Packed npx/bunx smoke passes all nine bundled packages. Independent installed Node and Bun consumers pass real plain-merge conflict/abort, readonly planning, audited and legacy-audit settlement, unaudited-terminal visibility, byte-identical retries, typed preview refusal and actual cherry-pick/revert non-attribution. Hosted checks and a new full review of the next pushed source remain the landing gate; publication waits for the next eligible daily release."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T10:18:04.160Z","harness:codex","Git operation identity evidence: upstream builtin/merge.c sets GITHEAD_<incoming object ID> before the merge strategy and ORIG_HEAD update (https://github.com/git/git/blob/master/builtin/merge.c). Real conflicting content-driver probes in both SHA-1 and SHA-256 observe that signal only for plain merge, while cherry-pick/revert can share stale HEAD/ORIG_HEAD and ours coordinates. The SDK records only kind/origin commit/blob, never incoming branch labels. If the signal is missing or malformed, capture stays undefined and no plain-merge abandonment audit is authorized. Existing real abort/restoration, active/changed-state, concurrency and interrupted-audit retry guards remain required."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T05:11:36.323Z","harness:codex","Git publishes MERGE_HEAD after content drivers execute. Capture plain-merge origin from matching HEAD/ORIG_HEAD and the exact ours blob; active-operation markers alone cannot capture that boundary. Settlement still rechecks inactive Git, exact HEAD/index/item and clean locked history."
  "2026-10-07T09:41:17.761Z","harness:codex","Matching HEAD, ORIG_HEAD and ours bytes establish origin coordinates, not operation identity. Git cherry-pick/revert reuse content drivers and may inherit matching stale ORIG_HEAD. Plain-merge capture additionally requires Git-generated GITHEAD_<incoming object ID>, including SHA-1/SHA-256. Missing signal fails closed; do not use customizable GIT_REFLOG_ACTION alone. Preserve readonly unsupported receipts and every existing audited rebase/plain-merge recovery guard."
